estion" "q-339872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=0,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=0-(-\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(y(2{x}^{3}+3)+{y}_{\\text{new}}(2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+3))\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}y(2{x}^{3}+3)+\\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}(2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{4}y(2{x}^{3}+3)+\\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}(2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+3) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{4}y(2{x}^{3}+7)+\\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}(2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}(2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+3) & =\\frac{1}{4}y(2{x}^{3}+7) \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}(1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}) & =\\frac{1}{4}y(2{x}^{3}+7) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y(2{x}^{3}+7)}{1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=0.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y(2{x}^{3}+7)}{1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}(2\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}+7)}{1-2\\cdot {0}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & ≈2.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(0)≈2.25.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067188/state.json" "file_sha256" "98381986de5c63f4a92736416863e9c4d9fce07b29e9bb957d3bba052038b804"} {"question" "q-339872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067188/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9446c68c60a0534a10a72f849a8cbe2e143d02ce1b73358e1b29ed25bed1591d"} {"question" "q-339872" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067188/state.json" "file_sha256" "98381986de5c63f4a92736416863e9c4d9fce07b29e9bb957d3bba052038b804"} {"question" "q-339872" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.13"] ["math" "1.44"] ["math" "2.25"] ["math" "2.75"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067188/state.json" "file_sha256" "98381986de5c63f4a92736416863e9c4d9fce07b29e9bb957d3bba052038b804"} {"question" "q-339872" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.25"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067188/state.json" "file_sha256" "98381986de5c63f4a92736416863e9c4d9fce07b29e9bb957d3bba052038b804"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2230 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
